            <notesStmt>
                <note type="project" target="#dat1">Whitman wrote this poem in response to the death of General Philip Henry Sheridan on August 5, 1888, and he prepared this manuscript for the printer sometime between that date and August 11, 1888, when Sheridan was buried.</note>
                <note type="work_relations" target="xxx.00393" cert="high">This poem was first published without title in the <hi rend="italic">New York Herald</hi> on <date when="1888-08-12">August 12, 1888</date>. Whitman later included it in <hi rend="italic">Good-Bye My Fancy</hi> (1891) with the title "Interpolation Sounds."</note>
            </notesStmt>
